    "problem": {
      "type": "content-columns",
      "settings": {
        "color_scheme": "paper",
        "layout": "list",
        "numbered": false,
        "row_density": "compact",
        "eyebrow": "The problem",
        "heading": "The boot is not the last line — and most wet feet are not earned on a mountain.",
        "lede": "<p>Hill days are long, the ground holds water, and a boot takes it from every direction at once. None of that is a fault in the boot. It is what happens to any waterproof shell worn for eight hours in weather.</p>"
      },
      "blocks": {
        "p1": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Wetting out is normal",
            "body": "<p>The outer soaks, the membrane stops moving vapour, and what felt waterproof at nine o'clock is heavy and cold by one. Reproofing delays it. It does not prevent it.</p>"
          }
        },
        "p2": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "The ground is wetter than the forecast",
            "body": "<p>Bog, tussock, a stream that has come up overnight. Most of what soaks a hill walker arrives below the ankle rather than from the sky.</p>"
          }
        },
        "p3": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Nothing dries on the hill",
            "body": "<p>There is no radiator at the halfway point. Wet at eleven means wet until the car park.</p>"
          }
        },
        "w-p1": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Grass holds more water than rain does",
            "body": "<p>Twenty minutes across a wet field in mesh trainers soaks a foot more thoroughly than an hour of walking in drizzle.</p>"
          }
        },
        "w-p2": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Trainers are built to breathe, not to seal",
            "body": "<p>The mesh that stops your feet cooking in July is an open door in November. It is doing exactly what it was designed to do.</p>"
          }
        },
        "w-p3": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "It is the same pair every day",
            "body": "<p>A hill walker's boots get a day off to dry out. The shoes you wear every morning do not.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "p1",
        "p2",
        "p3",
        "w-p1",
        "w-p2",
        "w-p3"
      ]
    },
    "answers": {
      "type": "content-columns",
      "settings": {
        "color_scheme": "ink",
        "layout": "list",
        "numbered": true,
        "eyebrow": "What answers it",
        "heading": "What is doing the work.",
        "head_note": "<p>The same sock we sell for everything else — there is no separate, lesser build for one activity. What changes is why each part of it matters here.</p>",
        "link_label": "The three layers, in section",
        "link_url": "/#construction"
      },
      "blocks": {
        "a1": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "The membrane is inside the sock",
            "body": "<p>A licensed Porelle® waterproof-breathable laminate, sealed between two knitted layers. Water that gets past the boot stops at the sock instead of at your skin.</p>"
          }
        },
        "a2": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Vapour still has somewhere to go",
            "body": "<p>The membrane is breathable in the outward direction, so sweat from a climb moves out rather than collecting against the foot.</p>"
          }
        },
        "a3": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Crew height, above the collar",
            "body": "<p>The cuff sits above the top of a low or mid boot, so the opening in the sock is not level with the opening in the boot.</p>"
          }
        },
        "w-a1": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "It works in the shoes you have",
            "body": "<p>There is nothing to buy twice. The same pair goes under trainers on Monday and under boots on Saturday.</p>"
          }
        },
        "w-a2": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Porelle®, named on the label",
            "body": "<p>A licensed third-party membrane rather than an unnamed laminate — the one specification in this category you can look up without taking our word for it.</p>"
          }
        },
        "w-a3": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Crew height, unisex sizing",
            "body": "<p>One height, sized in bands rather than by gender, so a household can share a size between them.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "a1",
        "a2",
        "a3",
        "w-a1",
        "w-a2",
        "w-a3"
      ]
    },
